# Version Management

## Purpose
Defines version control patterns and semantic versioning guidelines for SND macros to track changes and maintain proper version history.

## Scope
This rule covers version increment patterns, change tracking, semantic versioning, and automation for version updates.

## Version Change Requirements

### Core Principle
**Every change to a script MUST result in a version increment.** No exceptions.

### When to Increment Version
```lua
-- ✅ REQUIRED - Increment version for ANY change:
-- - Bug fixes
-- - New features
-- - Configuration changes
-- - Code refactoring
-- - Documentation updates
-- - Performance improvements
-- - Dependency updates
-- - UI changes
-- - Logic modifications
```

## Semantic Versioning Pattern

### Version Format
```lua
-- Use semantic versioning: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
version: 1.0.0
--        │ │ │
--        │ │ └── PATCH: Bug fixes, minor corrections
--        │ └──── MINOR: New features, enhancements
--        └────── MAJOR: Breaking changes, major rewrites
```

### Version Increment Guidelines

#### PATCH Version (1.0.0 → 1.0.1)
```lua
-- Increment PATCH for:
-- - Bug fixes
-- - Typo corrections
-- - Minor code cleanup
-- - Performance optimizations
-- - Documentation updates
-- - Configuration value adjustments
-- - Error message improvements

-- Example changes:
-- - Fixed inventory check logic
-- - Corrected spelling in echo messages
-- - Optimized wait times
-- - Updated comments
```

#### MINOR Version (1.0.0 → 1.1.0)
```lua
-- Increment MINOR for:
-- - New features
-- - New configuration options
-- - Enhanced functionality
-- - New plugin integrations
-- - Additional error handling
-- - New state machine states
-- - UI improvements

-- Example changes:
-- - Added new crafting recipe support
-- - Added configuration for wait times
-- - Enhanced error recovery
-- - Added new plugin integration
```

#### MAJOR Version (1.0.0 → 2.0.0)
```lua
-- Increment MAJOR for:
-- - Breaking changes to configuration
-- - Complete rewrites
-- - Removed features
-- - Changed plugin dependencies
-- - Modified core behavior
-- - Incompatible changes

-- Example changes:
-- - Changed configuration structure
-- - Removed deprecated features
-- - Changed plugin requirements
-- - Modified core state machine logic
```

## Version Update Patterns

### Manual Version Updates
```lua
-- Always update version in metadata header
--[=====[
[[SND Metadata]]
author: 'Your Name'
version: 1.0.1  -- ← UPDATE THIS
description: Brief description of what the macro does
plugin_dependencies:
- PluginName1
configs:
  SettingName:
    default: "defaultValue"
    description: What this setting does
[[End Metadata]]
--]=====]
```

### Version Change Documentation
```lua
-- Document version changes in comments
-- Version 1.0.1 - Fixed inventory space check logic
-- Version 1.1.0 - Added support for new crafting recipes
-- Version 2.0.0 - BREAKING: Changed configuration structure
```

## Automated Version Suggestions

### Cursor Rule Integration
```lua
-- When making changes, Cursor should suggest:
-- 1. Identify change type (bug fix, feature, breaking)
-- 2. Suggest appropriate version increment
-- 3. Update metadata header
-- 4. Add change documentation
```

### Change Type Detection
```lua
-- Bug Fix Indicators:
-- - "fix", "correct", "resolve", "repair"
-- - Error handling improvements
-- - Logic corrections
-- → Increment PATCH

-- Feature Indicators:
-- - "add", "new", "enhance", "improve"
-- - New functionality
-- - Additional options
-- → Increment MINOR

-- Breaking Change Indicators:
-- - "remove", "delete", "change structure"
-- - Configuration changes
-- - Dependency changes
-- → Increment MAJOR
```

## Version History Tracking

### Changelog Pattern
```lua
-- Add version history section to scripts
--[=====[
## Version History
- v1.0.0 - Initial release
- v1.0.1 - Fixed inventory space check
- v1.1.0 - Added new crafting recipe support
- v1.1.1 - Fixed recipe validation logic
- v2.0.0 - BREAKING: Restructured configuration system
--]=====]
```

### Change Documentation
```lua
-- Document each change clearly
-- Version 1.0.1 (2024-01-15)
-- - Fixed: Inventory space check was failing for edge cases
-- - Changed: Wait time reduced from 2s to 1s for better performance
-- - Added: Additional error logging for debugging

-- Version 1.1.0 (2024-01-20)
-- - Added: Support for new crafting recipes (X, Y, Z)
-- - Added: Configuration option for custom wait times
-- - Enhanced: Error recovery with automatic retry logic
```

## Version Validation

### Pre-Release Checklist
```lua
-- Before releasing any script version:
-- [ ] Version number incremented in metadata
-- [ ] Change type identified (PATCH/MINOR/MAJOR)
-- [ ] Version history updated
-- [ ] Changes documented
-- [ ] No breaking changes without MAJOR increment
-- [ ] Configuration changes properly handled
```

### Version Consistency
```lua
-- Ensure version consistency across:
-- - Metadata header
-- - Version history comments
-- - Any external documentation
-- - Git commit messages (if using version control)
```

