## Best Practices

### 1. Always Increment Version
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Every change gets version bump
-- Fixed typo in error message
-- version: 1.0.0 → 1.0.1

-- ❌ BAD - Changes without version increment
-- Fixed typo in error message
-- version: 1.0.0 (unchanged)
```

### 2. Use Semantic Versioning
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Proper semantic versioning
-- Bug fix: 1.0.0 → 1.0.1
-- New feature: 1.0.1 → 1.1.0
-- Breaking change: 1.1.0 → 2.0.0

-- ❌ BAD - Random version numbers
-- Bug fix: 1.0.0 → 1.0.3
-- New feature: 1.0.3 → 1.2.1
```

### 3. Document Changes
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Clear change documentation
-- Version 1.0.1 - Fixed inventory space validation logic

-- ❌ BAD - No change documentation
-- Version 1.0.1 - Updated
```

### 4. Consistent Versioning
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Consistent across all files
-- Script A: version 1.0.1
-- Script B: version 1.0.1 (if same change type)

-- ❌ BAD - Inconsistent versioning
-- Script A: version 1.0.1
-- Script B: version 1.0.0 (same changes)
```

## Error Prevention

### Common Version Mistakes
```lua
-- ❌ AVOID - Forgetting to increment version
-- Making changes without updating version number

-- ❌ AVOID - Wrong increment type
-- Adding new feature but only incrementing PATCH

-- ❌ AVOID - Breaking changes without MAJOR increment
-- Changing configuration structure but only incrementing MINOR

-- ❌ AVOID - Inconsistent versioning
-- Different scripts with different version numbers for same changes
```

### Version Validation Rules
```lua
-- Automated checks should verify:
-- 1. Version number is present in metadata
-- 2. Version follows semantic versioning format
-- 3. Version is incremented from previous version
-- 4. Change type matches version increment
-- 5. Version history is updated
```

